# Object/field label translation (inside the canonical deploy command)

English labels for custom objects, the standard Name field, and custom fields
are produced, validated, planned, deployed, and verified through the existing
orchestrator. Provenance is also stamped on standard field rows (OwnerId,
CreatedDate, …). There is no second translation command.

```
python scripts/prep_deploy.py --org "<ORG>" --tabs "<tab1>,<tab2>" --phase deploy \
    --apply-translations
```

`--apply-translations` is the gated sheet write of the translation batch
(preview first, then confirm). It is not a second pipeline.

## Flow (inserted into prep_deploy, not a fork)

1. Live fetch of **selected `--tabs` only**.
2. Structural pre-validation + collect labels that need English.
3. Provider preflight: DeepL MCP if healthy, else Google Sheets `GOOGLETRANSLATE`.
   One provider per batch; never mix. DeepL failure after preflight is fatal
   (no Google fallback, no partial write).
4. Terminology: API-name match → standard field map → unique JA→EN on the
   selected tabs → provider.
5. One confirmation for the complete sheet-write batch (headers, EN, provenance).
6. Stale-check immediately before write. Recalc + read calculated Google values.
7. Existing `validate_sheet.py` **plus** translation ERRORs (blank/invalid EN
   never degrades to WARN).
8. Fresh org snapshot (Tooling fields + CustomObjectTranslation).
9. Immutable plan → schema XML + patched COT XML (org tree preserved).
10. Manifest **from the plan**. Check-only, then real deploy, then live exact-EN verify.
11. Sync state (org Id) only after verification succeeds.

## Sheet columns (header-driven)

- `Field Label (EN)`
- `Translation Provenance` — one cell immediately to the right of
  `Field Label (EN)`: `origin | ja-sha256 | generated-at`
  (`manual` / `inventory` / `deepl` / `google`). Stamped on custom **and**
  standard field rows. Legacy three-column headers are still read if present,
  never created.

Missing headers occupy spare `FreeColumnGDC*` cells after confirmation.
Japanese source changes (hash mismatch) replace previous English, including
former `manual` values. Unchanged JA is never retranslated because DeepL later
became available.

## Out of initial scope

Picklist values, relationship labels, help text, LWC/Flow/Custom Labels, layouts,
record types.

## Must not

- Write English into Japanese `CustomField.label`.
- Deploy blank translations.
- Use API name / JA source / placeholder / formula text as English.
- Scan or modify tabs that were not selected.
- Change `fetch_sheet.py` / `write_back.py` Google authentication.
- Call Cloud Translation API, a service-account JSON, or an LLM to generate
  English labels.
- Use Cursor/Claude/another LLM to generate translations.
